 "summary": "A series of four-diode full-wave bridges in the UMSB package, rated 3.0 A average output and 100 A peak surge. Seven voltage grades run from 50 V (MSB30A) to 1000 V (MSB30M) repetitive peak reverse voltage; all other ratings are shared. They are meant for general single-phase rectification on printed circuit boards. MSB30M is the 1000 V grade.",
 "key_figures": [
  [
   "Repetitive peak reverse voltage VRRM",
   "50, 100, 200, 400, 600, 800 or 1000 V (MSB30M: 1000 V)"
  ],
  [
   "Average rectified output current IF(AV)",
   "3.0 A, 60 Hz sine, resistive load"
  ],
  [
   "Peak forward surge current IFSM",
   "100 A, 8.3 ms half-sine"
  ],
  [
   "I²t for fusing",
   "42 A²s at 8.3 ms"
  ],
  [
   "Forward voltage VF",
   "1.1 V max at IF = 3.0 A"
  ],
  [
   "Reverse current IR",
